* Bug 1: stale en-passant state after make/unmake
  (description generated by gpt)
  applyMoveImpure is reversible: applying the same pieceMovement again is used
  to unmake the move. This requires each generated move to encode the board's
  current en-passant state so that the metadata is restored correctly during
  unmake.

  One move-generation helper initialized the move's enPassantState to -1 instead
  of board.enPassantState. As a result, piece placement was restored correctly
  after make/unmake, but the en-passant metadata could become stale. Perftree
  then generated 1-2 illegal extra en-passant captures in some branches.

  This did not reproduce by loading the later FEN directly, because the bug was
  not in move generation from a clean position. It only appeared after a
  make/unmake sequence created a board with correct pieces but incorrect
  en-passant state.

  Incorrect:
  @code cpp
  int8_t enPassantState {-1};
  @end

  Correct:
  @code cpp
  int8_t enPassantState {board.enPassantState};
  @end

  Location:
  addAttacksToStack218(...)

  Regression test:
  TODO

  Fixed in:
  TODO
